# The Vercel build only needs vercel-news/ (the app) and docs/ (the daily shell
# that build.js copies into public/). Everything else here is the Python scanner
# and its data — excluding it keeps the upload small and stops Vercel from
# trying to detect a Python project at the root.
#
# Note the directory entries below: these follow gitignore semantics, where a
# file cannot be re-included if its parent directory is itself excluded. The
# bare `!vercel-news` / `!docs` lines are what make the `!.../**` lines work.
*
!vercel-news
!vercel-news/**
# life.askakshay.com. Its build.js reads docs/desk.html, which is already
# allow-listed below for the /desk route on news.askakshay.com.
!vercel-life
!vercel-life/**
!docs
!docs/index.html
!docs/alerts.json
# The build stamp open tabs poll to notice they are showing yesterday's paper.
# It is allow-listed by name like the two above — omit it and build.js finds
# nothing to copy, /edition.json 404s, and every tab silently stops checking.
!docs/edition.json
# The machine-readable edition the Telegram bot reads for /ideas and /desk.
# Allow-listed BY NAME like every other file here — omit it and the bot's
# section commands silently 404 with no error anywhere.
!docs/today.json
# The Rs 1 crore order book the client-rendered site sizes its Book
# section from. Allow-listed BY NAME like every other file here.
!docs/mandate.json
# The client-rendered site: shell + renderer.
!docs/v2.html
!docs/v2.js
!docs/v2-core.js
!docs/life.html
!docs/life.js
# The Nifty 500 research screen #stocks fetches lazily. Same by-name rule: omit
# it and the section falls back to its server-rendered top 25 forever, with the
# only symptom a console warning nobody reads.
!docs/screen.json
# The detail half of the screen, fetched only when a reader opens a company.
# Same by-name rule: omit it and every detail sheet renders its table row and
# nothing else, with only a console warning to say why.
!docs/screen-detail.json
# The senior-finance job feed, written daily by jobs.py. Same by-name rule:
# omit it and the careers section fetches a 404 and renders empty, with only a
# console warning to say why.
!docs/jobs.json
# The health of every dataset on the site, machine-readable. Same by-name rule:
# omit it and /data-health.json 404s — and the one artefact whose entire job is
# to be reachable when the page is under suspicion becomes unreachable.
!docs/data-health.json
# The page script. Without this the site renders and does nothing.
!docs/app.js
!docs/robots.txt
!docs/sitemap.xml
!docs/manifest.webmanifest
!docs/icon.svg
!docs/og.png
!docs/desk.html
!docs/fonts
!docs/fonts/**

node_modules
smoke_runner.cjs

# Never ship the ledger or its WAL, even by accident.
signals.db
signals.db-shm
signals.db-wal
.env
